algorithms.pseudocode:
Input: WeightedClosureSystem S, Boundary B
Output: Set of (signature, weight) pairs

function ExtractBoundaryData(S, B):
    data = {}
    for each generator g in S:
        sig = S.out(g) ∩ B
        data.add((sig, S.weight(g)))
    return data

Time: O(|G| · |X|)
Space: O(|G| · |B|)

Input: Systems S1, S2 in normal form, Boundary B
Output: Bijection e: G1 → G2 or NONE

function FindGaugeEquiv(S1, S2, B):
    // Build lookup tables
    for each g in S1.generators:
        key = (boundarySig(B, S1, g), S1.weight(g))
        table1[key] = g
    for each g in S2.generators:
        key = (boundarySig(B, S2, g), S2.weight(g))
        table2[key] = g

    // Check key sets match
    if keys(table1) ≠ keys(table2):
        return NONE

    // Build bijection
    equiv = {}
    for each key in table1:
        equiv[table1[key]] = table2[key]
    return equiv

Time: O(|G| · |B|)
Space: O(|G|)
